{"ts": "2026-11-23T05:08:08.492259Z", "run_id": "r-20261123T0346Z-0270", "unit": "openspec:add-mcp-client", "seq": 88, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-001", "id": "Q-001", "status": "answered", "reason": "Read the frozen test: findOutput() at line 34 returns a schema with required [\"vendor_id\",\"status\"] and additionalProperties false; line 539 asserts find.output deep-equals it; lines 540-541 validate {} against it. Read src/interpreter/schema.ts: checkSchema runs ajv.compile(schema) then validate(data) and answers ok false when validation fails, so {} fails on required. The spec requires the output to keep the server's outputSchema except the dropped pattern, $id and $anchor, so the test's own line 539 forbids a production fix that drops required. The clarifier's data { vendor_id: \"V-ACME\", status: \"active\" } is a valid instance (two strings, no extra properties) and matches A1's answer in the spec, so both checkSchema calls pass and the scenario \"two compiles of the output pass\" is checked.", "called": true, "tasks": ["2.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.8672839999999999, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "427d37e347b4f29e2e36af1391dae22e5efd2d3f056a5711991d7eae0ea5b2fe", "checked": [{"ref": "src/tools/mcp/surface.test.ts:38", "quote": "required: [\"vendor_id\", \"status\"],", "claim": "findOutput() requires vendor_id and status, so the empty object does not satisfy it."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/surface.test.ts:539", "quote": "assert.deepEqual(find.output, findOutput());", "claim": "The test itself asserts the normalised output keeps the required members, so production cannot drop them."}, {"ref": "src/tools/mcp/surface.test.ts:540", "quote": "assert.equal(checkSchema(find.output, {}).ok, true);", "claim": "The two assertions validate the empty object against the schema and expect ok true, which contradicts line 539."}, {"ref": "src/interpreter/schema.ts:11", "quote": "const validate = ajv.compile(schema as object);\n    if (validate(data)) return { ok: true };", "claim": "checkSchema compiles the schema and validates the data, answering ok false when the data violates required."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-mcp/spec.md#scenario-schemas-are-normalised-first", "quote": "M13 drops `pattern: \"^(a+)+$\"` and `$id` (two compiles of the output pass)", "claim": "The scenario only asks that two compiles of the output pass, which valid data satisfies."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-mcp/spec.md#requirement-a-servers-hints-never-decide-an-effect-or-retry-safety", "quote": "`structured` with the server's `outputSchema`", "claim": "The output schema is the server's outputSchema, so required stays and the test data must satisfy it."}]}
